# Measurement artefacts that are evidence, not scratch: the scored pool board and
# the cheap-vs-physics board are what the metric claims rest on, and a claim whose
# numbers cannot be re-read is the thing this workshop argues against.
!workshops/idetc26/tools/*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repository is code plus documentation written for someone outside it.
# Everything below is one of: a rendered figure, a solver dump, a cached
# measurement, or a note written for the next session rather than for a reader.
# All of it was tracked at some point and none of it should have been --
# 84e6ff5 alone swept in 88 MB of PNGs and FEniCS output beside a code change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Working notes and session handoffs: internal, superseded quickly, and not
# documentation anybody outside this repo should be handed.
claude_markdowns/

# Rendered outputs and their sources. Figures are regenerated by
# engiopt/lvae/paper_figures.py from data the cluster writes; the paper and the
# deck live with the manuscript, not with the library.
paper/
talk/
case_study_figs/
opt_frames/
engiopt/vanilla_lvae/
templates/

# Solver scratch. FEniCS writes these beside whatever directory it ran in.
*.xdmf
*.h5
output_by_pid/

# Cached measurements and scratch analysis. Boards under workshops/idetc26/tools
# are exempted above because they are evidence.
candidates_lv.json
candidates_by_cfg.json
ladder_checkpoints.json
*.ipynb_checkpoints/

.DS_Store

# Working notes from AI sessions. Useful locally, never part of the project.
claude_markdowns/
.claude/

# Scratch design cache written by the workshop tools; regenerated on demand.
idetc26_work/

# These carry a plaintext WANDB_API_KEY. Ignored so no `git add -A` can publish
# it; the key itself still needs rotating, and the scripts need it read from the
# environment before they can be tracked.
run_distortion_capture.sh
run_eval_all.sh
run_eval_cgan_sweep.sh
run_eval_missing.sh
run_eval_thermoelastic.sh
run_lv_only_eval.sh
run_lv_only_eval_sweep.sh

# Cluster job scripts. Machine-specific -- partitions, module loads, account
# names and paths that only mean something on Euler -- and they source secrets
# from $HOME/.engiopt_secrets, so they are kept out of a public repo entirely.
slurm/
*.slurm

# Scratch debugging notebook: 2.8 MB of embedded outputs, referenced by nothing.
# Listed as well as untracked -- a rule added after a file is tracked is inert.
Engi_debugger.ipynb
